&lt;h1&gt;Marketing Technology Program Manager&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Marketing Operations team is responsible for the systems, processes, and data infrastructure that power Stripe&#39;s global marketing engine. We partner closely with Growth Product, Growth Marketing, Regional Demand and Field Marketing, Lifecycle Marketing, Sales Development, and Marketing Technology teams to ensure campaigns are executed with precision with as much automation as possible, prospect and performance data are accurate and actionable, and our marketing technology stack operates at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are systems thinkers and operational leaders focused on improving the workflows, tooling, data quality, and processes that enable marketing and sales teams to move faster and more effectively. Our work spans campaign operations, marketing automation, prospect data management, lead management, pre-and post event operations, cross-functional program delivery, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Marketing Technology Program Manager. This role sits at the intersection of technology, data, and program management, and it requires someone who can move fluidly between strategic planning and hands-on execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive technology programs that power Stripe&#39;s marketing engine. Lead cross-functional programs with product, engineering, and marketing stakeholders. Drive improvements and innovation through AI, process automation, and 1st and 3rd party tools. Deliver the systems that enable marketing teams to move faster, continuously improve performance, and remove bottlenecks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the program manager for 1-2 initiatives at a time. Examples include the following.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital channel effectiveness: Improve digital campaign performance through personalization, content optimization, audience optimization. Include recommendation system interlock.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measurement: Give every campaign a consistent identity; connect marketing activity, spend, engagement, leads, and downstream outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account-Based Marketing (ABM): Identify target accounts, coordinate account-based campaigns, personalize account experiences, capture engagement, measure account penetration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Online Event Production &amp;amp; Community: Digital event promotion, registration, online attendance, content delivery, community engagement, and follow-up/measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program management responsibilities include&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end program delivery for initiatives; maintain program communications, track milestones, lead cross-functional workstreams, and provide regular updates on roadmap progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead programs to address recurring marketing process and technology challenges; define objectives, success metrics, and build repeatable processes that scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product and engineering teams to scope business requirements, coordinate discovery, and translate operational needs into product requirements for internal tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead requirements, selection, contracting, implementation, and adoption of third party software; drive new custom features in the company’s implementation of third party software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate review cycles, pilots, and feedback collection during program execution; summarize required changes, identify launch-blocking issues, and escalate risks as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive ongoing operations improvements through process innovation, automation, and the adoption of AI-powered tools to increase productivity and transform workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain scalable documentation and support coordination with offshore production teams and cross-functional partners across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in B2B marketing operations/technology or a related program management role in a high-growth technology environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience working day-to-day on some or all of the following: marketing automation platforms, CRM platforms, audience targeting and personalization, marketing campaign measurement, account based marketing, and online events (webinars)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in end-to-end program management of cross-functional marketing, sales, and engineering initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI agents, including examples of agents you have deployed and examples of ways you are using AI on a daily basis beyond chat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience doing your own analysis using queries, dashboards, and AI and partnering with analysts and data scientists for more complex analytics needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience defining your own scope and goals and collaborating with a distributed, global team to deliver on them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to convey complex operational concepts to diverse stakeholders across marketing, sales, and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing prospect or marketing database programs, including data enrichment, hygiene, and growth using first-party and third-party data sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience with marketing technology systems and platforms, including Marketo, customer data platforms, marketing channel and campaign measurement and attribution, account based marketing platforms, and online event platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selecting and managing third-party software in a B2B marketing context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing AI tools to improve marketing operations workflows and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with global teams on a day-to-day basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of data privacy and compliance frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the financial services, payments, or B2B software industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Product Manager to join the Vercel cloud product team. You will own the Storage product portfolio where applications and agents keep their data on Vercel. That covers Blob for blob storage, Drives for persistent filesystems, and future database and key value storage products. This is a hybrid role based in San Francisco, and you’ll report to the Product Lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re based within a pre-determined commuting distance of one of our offices (SF, NY, London, or Berlin), the role includes in-office anchor days on Monday, Tuesday, and Friday. If you&#39;re located beyond that distance, the role is fully remote. For location-specific details, please connect with our recruiting team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product vision, strategy, and multi-year roadmap for Vercel’s storage portfolio (blob storage, persistent filesystems, database, and key/value storage).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure storage products integrate seamlessly with the rest of Vercel’s cloud (Functions, backend services, Sandboxes, Daemons) to enable fully functional applications and agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and hold the bar for performance, availability, and durability across the portfolio, and make the call when those goals trade off against speed or cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape pricing and packaging for storage so it scales with customers from hobbyist to large Enterprises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Design, and DX to ship primitives that other Vercel product teams build on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with Enterprise customers and the field to unblock adoption on scale, compliance, and data locality and encryption requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use usage, performance, and reliability data to decide what to build next and what to stop doing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve shipped storage, database, or data infrastructure products, such as object storage, relational databases, or key-value stores.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can go deep on each storage solution and their tradeoffs, and explain them clearly to engineers and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve owned multiple connected product areas and set direction that other product teams built against.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve worked directly with Enterprise customers on data and storage requirements and turned them into roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus If You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked at cloud provider or data storage provider.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have an engineering background or have built software yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with compliance and security requirements in enterprise procurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible Time Off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $208,000 - $312,000. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
